From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tinycast Recipe <recipe@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:45:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] tinycast-space 0018: entry deeplinks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`tinycast://open?id=<percent-encoded AppEntry.id>` runs a launcher entry through `LauncherCoordinator.launch`, as Return does (snippets expand at the caret instead); unknown ids show a HUD. Routed in `AppCore.handleOpenURL` after confetti and themes. Every entry's ⌘K menu gets *Copy Deeplink* (extension commands copy `tinycast://extensions/<owner>/<ext>/<cmd>`). No `arguments` are read, meetings and query-driven commands get no link, and system actions keep their confirmations. New `EntryDeepLink.swift`, `EntryDeepLinkActions.swift`, `entry-deeplink-test`. Declined upstream (#1005). A link that activated Tinycast first hands focus back (`NSApp.deactivate()`, then up to 500 ms for another app to come forward; no observer), so window commands, snippets and paste act on the app the link came from (after [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/b82afd94)).

Origin: tinycast-space 0018-entry-deeplinks.patch @ ffccfc3
